# SOLID Principles

Apply when change is expensive due to coupling. Skip for throwaway scripts or forever-single implementations.

- **SRP:** one reason to change; split validation/persistence/notification; fat test classes signal violation.
- **OCP:** grow via new types/strategies, not endless if/switch edits to one method.
- **LSP:** subtypes must honor the contract; decorators/caches preserve observable behavior.
- **ISP:** prefer narrow interfaces clients actually use; no fat “god” ports.
- **DIP:** depend on abstractions at boundaries; inject collaborators; domain does not import frameworks.

Ask “what is the second implementation?” (test fake counts). Prefer extract over premature abstraction.
